    {
      "_id": "vWaU1PJbd5VJ7nUC",
      "name": "Soul Simulacrum",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/svg/item-bag.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>An ur'zul contains 1d8+1 different souls, with a minimum of two needed to maintain its form. It knows all the memories of the souls it has devoured. As a bonus action, the ur'zul can extrude a piece of itself that assumes the appearance of one Medium or smaller creature who's soul it has devoured. The visage appears, feels, and sounds exactly like the creature it impersonates, though it smells faintly of sulfur. Each visage is tethered to the Ur'zul by a stand of sickly white flesh that can extend up to 120 feet from the ur'zul. While the ur'zul has a visage extruded, it can see through its senses. The ur'zul can have up to three visages extruded from its body. The sickly tendrils are immune to damage, but servered if there is no opening at least 1 inch wide between the visage and the ur'zul. A visage disappears if the tether is servered.\"</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
